                "id": "cmi-terminal-forensics-debit-rejection",
                "heading": "The Forensic Reality: Why Moroccan CMI Terminals Reject Debit Cards & Neobanks",
                "content": "Every day at Marrakech Menara (RAK), Casablanca Mohammed V (CMN), and Agadir Al Massira (AGA), hundreds of European and UK travelers find their prepaid rental vouchers voided at the counter. The root cause is a fundamental technical mismatch between European payment habits and Moroccan banking infrastructure.\n\nIn Morocco, 98% of card payment terminals are operated by the **Centre Monétique Interbancaire (CMI)** or Naps. When a rental agent processes a security deposit (known locally as a *caution* or *pré-autorisation*), the CMI terminal does not take your money; it executes an offline/online credit line freeze (ISO 8583 authorization hold) valid for up to 30 days.\n\n### How the BIN Check Blocks Your Card\nWhen you tap or insert your card, the CMI terminal reads the first 6 to 8 digits—the **Bank Identification Number (BIN)**. \n- **True Credit Cards (`CRÉDIT`):** Backed by a revolving bank credit line. The CMI terminal locks 10,000 to 25,000 MAD (approx. €920 to €2,300) seamlessly.\n- **Debit Cards (`DÉBIT`) & Neobanks:** Cards issued by **Revolut, Monzo, Starling, Wise, N26, and Boursorama** (unless explicitly configured as *Débit Différé*) carry a Debit or Prepaid BIN. Even if you have €15,000 sitting in your Revolut account, the CMI pre-authorization protocol rejects the hold or converts it into a **direct sale withdrawal (*Encaissement*)**.\n\nMost international franchises at Moroccan airports forbid their staff from executing a direct debit withdrawal for a deposit because refunding an international debit charge costs the agency **2.8% to 3.5% in non-recoverable CMI merchant fees** plus foreign exchange slippage.\n\n| Card Type / Issuer | Card Face Marking | CMI Pre-Auth (Hold) | Airport Broker Acceptance | Verified Local Fleet Acceptance |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Traditional Credit Card** (Amex, Visa/MC Credit) | `CREDIT` or `DÉBIT DIFFÉRÉ` | **Pass** (Instant Hold) | Accepted at face value | Accepted (Zero fee) |\n| **UK/EU High-Street Debit** (Barclays, Lloyds, BNP) | `DEBIT` | **Fail** (Pre-auth blocked) | Rejected (Forces SCDW buyout) | Accepted via Cash or POS Sale |\n| **Neobanks** (Revolut, Monzo, Wise, N26) | `DEBIT` / `PREPAID` | **Hard Fail** | Strictly Rejected | Accepted for Rental Fee + Cash Deposit |\n| **French Dual Cards** (Carte Bleue) | `CRÉDIT / DÉBIT` | **Conditional** (Must select Credit) | Accepted if `Débit Différé` | Accepted |\n\nIf you arrive at an airport multinational desk with a voucher from Rentalcars, DiscoverCars, or Expedia and present a debit card, the agent will declare you in breach of the Terms & Conditions. You will lose your prepaid booking deposit unless you submit to their counter upsell.",
