                "heading": "The Airport Desk Trap: How an €8/Day Broker Deal Becomes €380 at Pickup",
                "content": "Understanding the economic business model of aggregator platforms (CarJet, DoYouSpain, DiscoverCars, VIPCars) is essential to protecting your travel budget. During shoulder season in Marrakech or Tangier, you will frequently see a **Dacia Sandero** or **Hyundai i10** advertised online for **€6 to €10 per day** (65 to 110 MAD/day).\n\nIn Morocco, a brand-new Dacia Sandero costs an agency approximately **145,000 MAD (€13,500)** to purchase, and commercial all-risk rental insurance (*Assurance Tous Risques Location*) costs roughly **9,500 to 12,000 MAD per year**. Mathematically, no fleet operator in Morocco can break even renting a vehicle at 80 MAD/day. \n\n### The Anatomy of the Counter Upsell\nLow-cost franchises (such as Green Motion, Surprice, Locationauto, Aircar, and gold-tier budget brokers) price cars below cost specifically to trap debit-card holders at the airport terminal desk. Here is the exact sequence that unfolds when your card fails the CMI `CRÉDIT` verification:\n\n1. **Voucher Invalidation:** The desk clerk points to clause 4.2 in your 14-page voucher PDF: *\"Main driver must present an embossed Credit Card in their own name with available funds of 14,000 MAD.\"*\n2. **The Third-Party Insurance Illusion:** You explain that you already bought \"Full Protection Insurance\" online via the broker (typically marketed by Allianz or AXA for €9/day). The clerk correctly informs you that broker insurance is merely a **reimbursement policy**—it does not replace the physical security deposit required to release the car keys.\n3. **The Mandatory SCDW Buyout:** To waive the credit card requirement and reduce the deposit to zero (or 3,000 MAD cash), the clerk forces you to purchase the agency's internal **Super Collision Damage Waiver (SCDW)** at the maximum walk-in tariff: **280 to 350 MAD (€26 to €32) per day**.\n\n### Real-World 7-Day Cost Audit (Dacia Sandero Stepway)\n| Cost Component | Online Broker \"Trap\" Route (With Debit Card) | Direct Local Transparent Operator (No Credit Card) |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Base 7-Day Rental Rate** | 650 MAD (€60) | 2,100 MAD (€195) |\n| **Online Broker \"Full Cover\"** | 700 MAD (€65 - Useless at counter) | 0 MAD (Included in transparent tier) |\n| **Forced Airport Counter SCDW** | 2,240 MAD (€210 - 320 MAD/day) | 0 MAD |\n| **Cross-Border/Airport Admin Fee** | 350 MAD (€32) | 0 MAD |\n| **Required Deposit at Pickup** | 3,000 MAD (Debit Sale + 3.5% Fee) | 3,000 MAD (Refundable Cash in EUR/MAD) |\n| **Total Out-of-Pocket Rental Cost** | **3,940 MAD (€367)** | **2,100 MAD (€195)** |\n\nBy attempting to save €100 online without a credit card, travelers systematically overpay by **€150 to €200** while starting their Moroccan road trip in a state of high stress after a 45-minute argument at the terminal.",
