                "id": "understanding-franchise-excess-tiers-morocco",
                "heading": "Decoding Moroccan Insurance Tiers: Why 'Tous Risques' Still Has a 15,000 MAD Liability",
                "content": "A critical misconception among foreign drivers renting without a credit card in Morocco is the meaning of the phrase **\"Assurance Tous Risques\" (All-Risk / Comprehensive Insurance)**. \n\nWhen a local agency tells you on WhatsApp, *\"Don't worry, the car has Assurance Tous Risques and you only leave €300 cash deposit,\"* many travelers falsely assume their maximum financial liability in a crash is capped at their €300 deposit.\n\n### The Difference Between Deposit (*Caution*) and Excess (*Franchise*)\nIn Moroccan automotive insurance underwritten by Wafa Assurance, RMA, AXA Assurance Maroc, or Sanlam, commercial rental policies operate on a **proportional or fixed deductible (*Franchise*)** system:\n1. **The Deposit (*Caution*):** The immediate cash or debit amount held by the agency (e.g., 3,000 to 5,000 MAD) to cover minor scratches, a cracked mirror (400 MAD), a missing parcel shelf, or returning the car with an empty tank.\n2. **The Insurance Excess (*Franchise d'Assurance*):** Your contractual legal liability in the event of a major at-fault collision (*Responsabilité engagée*), rollover, or total vehicle theft.\n\nStandard Moroccan rental contracts set the default **Franchise between 10,000 MAD and 20,000 MAD (€920 to €1,850)**, or 10% to 15% of the vehicle's insured catalog value (*Valeur Vénale*). \n\n### 2026 Moroccan Vehicle Deposit & Excess Benchmark\n| Vehicle Model | Typical Cash/Debit Deposit | Standard Contractual Excess (*Franchise*) | Reduced Excess Option (SCDW +80 MAD/day) | Undercarriage & Glass Note |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Dacia Sandero Stepway** | 3,000 MAD (€300) | 10,000 MAD (€920) | 2,500 MAD (€230) | Tires/Glass excluded unless specified |\n| **Renault Clio 5 Automatic** | 4,000 MAD (€380) | 12,000 MAD (€1,100) | 3,000 MAD (€280) | Common curb rash target on alloys |\n| **Dacia Duster 4x4** | 5,000 MAD (€480) | 15,000 MAD (€1,400) | 4,000 MAD (€380) | Strict off-road (*Piste*) exclusions apply |\n\n### The 3 Mandatory Exclusions to Check on Your Contract\nEven if you pay extra to reduce your excess to match your cash deposit, virtually every Moroccan insurance underwriter enforces three non-negotiable exclusions unless you hold a dedicated **Bris de Glace & Pneumatiques** rider:\n- **Windshield & Glass (*Bris de Glace*):** Loose gravel kicked up by trucks on the N9 (Marrakech to Ouarzazate over the Tizi n'Tichka pass) frequently chips windshields. A replacement windshield on a Renault Clio 5 costs **1,800 to 2,600 MAD** locally.\n- **Tires & Rims (*Pneumatiques et Jantes*):** Hitting a pothole (*nid-de-poule*) after seasonal rains in the Rif or Atlas Mountains is classified as driver negligence (*faute de conduite*), not an insured collision. A torn Continental or Michelin tire costs **900 to 1,300 MAD**.\n- **Unpaved Tracks (*Conduite sur Piste*):** Taking a 2WD Dacia Sandero or Renault Clio 5 onto unpaved gravel tracks (such as the road to Cathedral Imsfrane or Erg Chigaga approaches) voids all insurance coverage immediately. Even in a **Dacia Duster 4x4**, verify written authorization for gravel tracks.",
