                "id": "five-step-proof-protocol",
                "heading": "The 5-Step Forensic Proof Protocol (Pickup to Drop-Off)",
                "content": "You do not defeat rental car scammers at the return bay; you neutralize them during the first eight minutes of pickup. When an agent sees a renter executing a structured fleet audit protocol, they immediately cross your contract off the easy-target list because they know any chargeback dispute with Visa or Mastercard will result in an instant merchant penalty against their CMI account.\n\n### Step 1: The Continuous 4K Timestamped Walkaround Video\nDo not rely exclusively on static photos; metadata can be stripped, and tight angles lack context. Set your smartphone camera to 4K at 60fps with the flash LED forced ON (even in daylight).\n- Start recording by filming the agency representative's face/hands, the rental office signboard, and the license plate (*plaque d'immatriculation*).\n- In one single, unbroken take (roughly 3 minutes), walk slowly clockwise around the vehicle.\n- Drop the camera to ankle height and pan continuously across the entire front lower bumper lip, side rocker panels (*bas de caisse*), and rear diffuser.\n- Zoom in on all four tire sidewalls (checking for *hernies* or bulges) and every alloy wheel rim.\n- Film the windshield from the outside at a 45-degree angle, lifting both wiper blades.\n\n### Step 2: The Trunk & Interior Mechanical Audit\nWhile still recording (or in a second continuous clip), open the trunk, lift the carpet mat, and film the spare tire, the wheel wrench (*clé démonte-roue*), the jack (*cric*), the warning triangle, and the reflective safety vest (*gilet jaune*). Sit in the driver's seat, turn the ignition completely on (engine running, not just accessory mode) to verify that no check-engine, ABS, or airbag warning lights remain illuminated, and record the exact odometer mileage and fuel gauge level.\n\n### Step 3: Forcing Contract Amendments (*L'État des Lieux*)\nNever accept verbal assurances like *\"Don't worry friend, small scratches under 3cm don't count in Morocco.\"* If it is not inked on the carbon-copy handover sheet, you are legally liable for it. Take the agent's pen and draw every single scuff, stone chip, interior cigarette burn, and missing hubcap directly onto the vehicle diagram. Write explicitly: **\"Voiture sale / mouillée à la prise en charge - sous réserve de contrôle à sec\"** (Car dirty/wet at pickup - subject to dry inspection) if handed a wet or dark car, and make the agent sign and stamp (*cachet de l'agence*) right next to your annotation.\n\n### Step 4: The WhatsApp Timestamp Anchor\nBefore driving out of the airport parking lot, send the full inspection video and photos of the signed contract directly to the rental agency's official WhatsApp number or email address. This creates an immutable, third-party server timestamp proving the exact condition of the vehicle before the tires ever touched public roads.\n\n### Step 5: The Mandatory Return Sign-Off & Pre-Auth Cancellation\nNever do a 'key-drop in the mailbox' return in Morocco unless you hold 0-deductible full coverage directly with a reputable operator. Arrive 20 minutes early for your return. Film a complete closing 4K walkaround video. Demand that the agent sign and stamp the return box of your contract with the exact phrase: **\"Véhicule restitué conforme - R.A.S. (Rien À Signaler)\"**. Finally, ask the agent to process an **Annulation de Pré-autorisation** on the CMI terminal and hand you the cancellation paper receipt.",
