                "id": "forensic-paper-trail-receipts-contracts",
                "heading": "The Forensic Paper Trail: Legal Receipts, Quittance & Deposit Protection",
                "content": "The primary anxiety travelers express on Reddit and TripAdvisor regarding cash car rentals in Morocco is simple: *\"If I pay cash, how do I prove I paid, and how do I guarantee my cash deposit is returned at 5:00 AM before my flight?\"*\n\nIn Moroccan commercial law (*Dahir des Obligations et Contrats - DOC, Articles 417 to 423*), a verbal acknowledgment of cash or an informal WhatsApp message holds dubious standing during an airport dispute with local tourist police (*Brigade Touristique*). You must secure a specific physical document trail before driving out of the airport parking lot.\n\n### The 4 Mandatory Elements of a Moroccan Cash Rental Contract\nEvery legally operating car rental company in Morocco (governed by the *Cahier des Charges des Agences de Location de Voitures sans Chauffeur* issued by the Ministry of Transport and Logistics) must provide a serialized, carbon-copy or digitally printed **Contrat de Location**. When paying cash, verify these four boxes before signing:\n\n1. **Montant Total TTC & Mention \"Payé en Espèces / Acquitté\":** The contract must state the exact total price inclusive of 20% VAT (*TTC*) and feature the handwritten mention **\"Payé en espèces\"** (Paid in cash) or a physical ink stamp reading **\"PAYÉ\"** directly over the financial summary box.\n2. **The Official Wet Stamp (Cachet de la Société):** Under Moroccan administrative culture, a signature without a company rubber stamp (*Cachet*) is legally incomplete. The stamp must clearly display the company's **ICE (Identifiant Commun de l'Entreprise - 15 digits)**, **RC (Registre de Commerce)**, and **IF (Identifiant Fiscal)**.\n3. **Dépôt de Garantie / Caution Explicit Entry:** If you leave a cash deposit (for example, €300 or 3,000 MAD), it must NEVER be kept \"off the books.\" The exact figure and currency symbol (e.g., *\"Caution: 300 Euros en espèces\"*) must be written inside the dedicated **Caution / Franchise** box on your copy of the contract.\n4. **Droit de Timbre (Fiscal Stamp Duty):** For formal accounting invoices (*Factures*) settled in cash, Moroccan tax law applies a 0.25% stamp duty. Transparent agencies absorb this internally within the quoted rate rather than surprising you at the hood of the car.\n\n### The Return Protocol: Signing the \"Décharge de Restitution\"\nWhen returning your Hyundai Tucson or Dacia Sandero Stepway at Marrakech, Casablanca, or Tangier airport and swapping the keys for your cash deposit, the exchange must be simultaneous. \n\nDo not hand over the vehicle registration papers (*Carte Grise* pack) and keys while waiting for an agent to \"go find change at the terminal.\" Confirm via WhatsApp 24 hours prior to drop-off that the agent meeting you at the departures drop-off zone (*Dépose-minute*) has your exact cash deposit envelope ready in the currency you deposited.",
