                "id": "financial-matrix-basic-cdw-vs-scdw-zero-excess",
                "heading": "Forensic Comparison: Basic CDW vs Super CDW vs Zero Excess",
                "content": "To make an objective financial decision, you must dissect the three tiers of risk transfer offered at Moroccan rental counters. Many international franchises operating at Agadir Al Massira or Casablanca airport utilize a stepping-stone pricing architecture: Basic CDW -> Partial Reduction (SLDW/SCDW) -> Total Waiver (Zero Excess / *Franchise Zéro*).\n\nAt transparent local operators like **ZwinCar**, the progression skips the ambiguous middle tier, offering direct upgrades from Basic CDW to comprehensive Zero Excess with ultra-low or zero deposit requirements.\n\n### 2026 Moroccan Fleet Insurance & Deposit Matrix\n\n| Vehicle Category & Model | Base CDW Franchise (Blocked on Card) | Daily Cost for Zero Excess (SCDW) | Franchise with Zero Excess | Admin Fee per Claim (*Frais de Dossier*) |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Economy** (Dacia Sandero / Clio 5) | 8,000 – 10,000 MAD (€735–€920) | 100 – 140 MAD (€9–€13) | 0 MAD | 0 MAD (ZwinCar) / 550 MAD (Majors) |\n| **Compact / Crossover** (Dacia Duster 4x4) | 12,000 – 15,000 MAD (€1,100–€1,380) | 150 – 180 MAD (€14–€16.50) | 0 MAD | 0 MAD (ZwinCar) / 650 MAD (Majors) |\n| **Mid-Size SUV** (Hyundai Tucson Auto) | 16,000 – 20,000 MAD (€1,470–€1,840) | 180 – 220 MAD (€16.50–€20) | 0 MAD | 0 MAD (ZwinCar) / 800 MAD (Majors) |\n| **Heavy 4x4** (Toyota Prado TX 7-Places) | 25,000 – 35,000 MAD (€2,300–€3,220) | 280 – 350 MAD (€25–€32) | 0 – 3,000 MAD | 0 MAD (ZwinCar) / 1,200 MAD (Majors) |\n\n### The Hidden 'Immobilization' & 'Dossier' Charges\nWhen auditing the fine print of budget aggregators at Marrakech and Fez airports, two unadvertised fees routinely cannibalize the deposits of Basic CDW holders:\n1. **Frais de Dossier (Administrative Damage Processing Fee):** Ranges from **550 MAD to 1,200 MAD (€50–€110)** charged simply for opening a damage file, regardless of whether the repair costs 300 MAD.\n2. **Frais d'Immobilisation (Loss of Use):** Under Article 264 of the Moroccan *Dahir des Obligations et Contrats (DOC)*, agencies legally bill you for the daily rental value of the car while it sits in the garage awaiting parts or repairs. If a headlight on a **Hyundai Tucson** takes 6 days to source from Casablanca, you are billed 6 additional rental days at the walk-in counter rate.\n\n**True Zero Excess (*Rachat Total de Franchise*)** explicitly waives both the administrative processing fee and the loss-of-use immobilization penalty.",
