                "content": "Even with full Zero Excess coverage, Moroccan insurance law mandates strict procedural compliance to keep your waiver valid. Failing to follow local traffic reporting protocols converts a 0 MAD liability into a full breach of contract.\n\n### Step 1: The 4-Minute Pick-Up Forensic Video\nBefore signing the *Fiche d'état du véhicule* at Casablanca, Marrakech, or Agadir airport:\n1. Record a continuous, timestamped 4K video walking slowly around the vehicle.\n2. **Zoom in on the four low-clearance danger zones:** the front bumper lower lip (often scraped on Moroccan high curbs), all four alloy rims, the windshield (check from an angle against the glare for micro-pits), and the roof.\n3. Open the trunk to verify the presence of the spare wheel (*roue de secours* or inflation kit), jack (*cric*), warning triangle, and reflective vest (*gilet jaune*—mandatory under the Moroccan Highway Code).\n4. Photograph the fuel gauge and odometer. In Morocco, fuel policies are strictly **Same-to-Same (*Niveau à Niveau*)**.\n\n### Step 2: The Accident Protocol (Keeping Zero Excess Valid)\nIf you are involved in a collision—or discover your parked car was scraped while you were having lunch in the Medina—do **not** move the vehicle or drive back to the agency assuming Zero Excess covers everything automatically.\n\n1. **Call the Fleet Agency Immediately:** Every legitimate contract has a 24/7 assistance number. Report the incident before taking action.\n2. **Two-Vehicle Minor Collision (No Injuries):** Fill out the yellow-and-blue **Constat Amiable** (European-style Joint Accident Report) located in your glovebox. Both drivers must sign it. If the other driver refuses or only speaks Darija/Tamazight, do not argue—call the authorities.\n3. **Urban vs. Rural Jurisdiction:**\n   - **Inside City Limits (*Périmètre Urbain*):** Call **19** (from a local SIM) or **112** (from any mobile) to summon the **Police (Sûreté Nationale)**. A specialized traffic officer (*Constatateur*) will draft an official report.\n   - **Outside Cities / Highways / Atlas Mountains:** Call **177** for the **Gendarmerie Royale**.\n4. **Parked Damage / Hit-and-Run:** Go to the nearest *Arrondissement de Police* to file a *Déclaration de perte/dégâts contre X* and obtain a stamped receipt (*Récépissé*). Handing this document to your rental agent at drop-off legally activates the underwriter's policy and ensures you walk away paying **0 MAD**.",
