                "id": "legal-framework-law-52-05",
                "heading": "Statutory Framework: Law 52-05 (Code de la Route) & Fine Structure",
                "content": "Moroccan road enforcement underwent a structural overhaul with the enactment of **Dahir n° 1-10-07 promulgating Law 52-05**, further updated by **Law 116-14** and enforced digitally by **NARSA** (*Agence Nationale de la Sécurité Routière*). Foreign tourists are subject to the exact same statutory penalties as residents, with one critical operational difference: because foreign licenses cannot be docked Moroccan demerit points (out of the standard 30-point domestic allocation), officers strictly enforce immediate payment of the *Amende Transactionnelle et Forfaitaire* (ATF).\n\nUnder the statutory grading system, traffic violations are divided into three tiers. If you pay on the spot (or within 24 hours at a designated *Trésorerie Générale* or via an officer's mobile TPE card terminal), you benefit from a statutory discount of roughly 43%. Do not confuse this discounted on-the-spot rate with a bribe; it is written directly into Article 219 of the Traffic Code.\n\n### 2026 Moroccan Traffic Fine Schedule (ATF Rates)\n\n| Violation Class | Common Offenses Included | Full Statutory Fine | Immediate Payment (Within 24h) | Paid Within 15 Days |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **1st Class** | Exceeding speed by 20–30 km/h; crossing a solid white line (*ligne continue*); failing to stop at a *STOP* (*Qif*) sign; driving in the opposite direction; dangerous overtaking. | 700 MAD (€65) | **400 MAD (€37)** | 500 MAD (€46) |\n| **2nd Class** | Exceeding speed by <20 km/h; handheld mobile phone use (including touching a mounted screen); failure to wear a seatbelt (front or rear passengers); failure to yield at a roundabout; entering a highway pedestrian zone. | 500 MAD (€46) | **300 MAD (€28)** | 350 MAD (€32) |\n| **3rd Class** | Exceeding speed by <10% in urban zones; faulty headlight/brake light bulb; improper urban parking; failure to display vehicle rental dossier when requested. | 300 MAD (€28) | **150 MAD (€14)** | 200 MAD (€18) |\n\n### Critical Legal Thresholds to Memorize\n* **Blood Alcohol Concentration (BAC):** Essentially **0.00%**. Morocco enforces a strict ban on driving under the influence. The technical legal breathalyzer threshold is 0.20 mg/l of exhaled air (0.40 g/l blood), which triggers an immediate criminal indictment, vehicle impoundment, and a fine between 5,000 and 10,000 MAD (€460–€925). Do not consume even half a glass of wine before driving.\n* **Speeding Over 30 km/h:** Exceeding the posted limit by 30 to 50 km/h elevates the offense out of the standard ATF bracket to a **1,400 MAD** fine (discounted to **800 MAD** if paid immediately). Exceeding by 50 km/h or more is a criminal misdemeanor requiring license confiscation and court appearance.\n* **Rear Seatbelts:** Since 2018, the *Gendarmerie Royale* actively checks rear passenger seatbelts at highway toll exits. Each unbuckled rear passenger incurs a separate 300 MAD immediate fine.",
