                "heading": "Jurisdictional Anatomy: Sûreté Nationale (DGSN) vs. Gendarmerie Royale",
                "content": "Understanding who is stopping you on Moroccan roads requires distinguishing between two entirely separate ministries and command chains. When exiting major hubs like Marrakech, Agadir, or Tangier, the transition from urban boulevards to national highways marks a hard jurisdictional boundary.\n\n**1. Direction Générale de la Sûreté Nationale (DGSN - Police):**\nOperating under the Ministry of the Interior, the DGSN controls all municipal perimeters, urban ring roads, and city entry/exit points (*Barrages Judiciaires*). You will identify them by their dark blue or black tactical uniforms, white utility vehicles (often Dacia Dokkers, Renault Trafics, or Skoda Octavias) with blue and red livery, and white traffic helmets for motorcycle units. Their primary mandate at city gates is national security, verifying vehicle registration anomalies, and screening commercial transport.\n\n**2. La Gendarmerie Royale:**\nOnce you pass the municipal boundary sign (marked by a red horizontal line through the city name), you enter the jurisdiction of the Gendarmerie Royale, an branch of the Royal Moroccan Armed Forces reporting to the Administration of National Defense. Gendarmes wear distinctive pearl-grey uniforms, white Sam Browne belts, and peaked caps (or blue berets). Their fleet consists of pearl-grey or dark-blue SUVs (Dacia Duster 4x4, Toyota Prado, Volkswagen Touareg) and BMW R1250RT motorcycles. The Gendarmerie controls all *Routes Nationales* (RN), *Routes Régionales* (RR), rural tracks, and the entire *Autoroutes du Maroc* (ADM) toll network.\n\n| Feature | Sûreté Nationale (DGSN) | Gendarmerie Royale |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Jurisdiction** | Urban areas, city limits, municipal gateways | Rural highways (RN/RR), mountain passes, ADM Tollways |\n| **Uniform Color** | Dark Navy Blue / Black Tactical | Pearl Grey with White Accents |\n| **Primary Focus** | Security screening, urban traffic violations, stolen vehicles | Speed enforcement (TruCAM), highway code compliance, rural security |\n| **Authority Type** | Civilian Police Force (Ministry of Interior) | Military Force (National Defense) |\n| **Tourist Interaction** | Extremely brief; usually waved through at city gates | Strict adherence to highway code; zero tolerance for speeding or lane violations |\n\nMany foreign drivers operate under the outdated belief that Moroccan roadblocks exist to harass tourists. In reality, since the modernization of the DGSN and Gendarmerie directives between 2018 and 2025, officers operate under strict orders to facilitate tourist transit. Over 90% of rental vehicles driven by foreigners are waved through fixed security checkpoints without document inspection—**provided the driver executes the approach protocol correctly.**",
