                "id": "southern-corridors-military-fiches-sahara",
                "heading": "Southern & Desert Corridors: Military Checkpoints and 'Fiches'",
                "content": "If your itinerary takes you into the deep south—specifically beyond **Guelmim, Tan-Tan, Tarfaya, Laâyoune, or Dakhla**, or along the Algerian border tracks near **Merzouga, Zagora, and Tata**—the nature of checkpoints shifts from traffic enforcement to territorial security.\n\nIn these zones, alongside the Gendarmerie Royale, you will encounter checkpoints manned by the **Forces Auxiliaires (Makhzen)** and the **Forces Armées Royales (FAR)**. Here, the inspection is never about your tire tread or speed; it is a strict census of foreign movements to ensure traveler safety in remote desert sectors.\n\n### The 'Fiche de Renseignements' Strategy\nAt every major town entrance south of Guelmim, an officer will ask for your passport and rental contract, walk into a guardhouse, and manually transcribe your details into a large ledger. This takes 5 to 10 minutes per checkpoint. \n\nExperienced Sahara drivers bypass this delay by preparing **15 to 20 printed 'Fiches de Police'** before departing Agadir or Marrakech. On a standard A4 page (cut into halves or quarters), print the following information clearly in French for each passenger, plus a photocopy of your passport photo page and entry stamp:\n* **Nom et Prénom** (Last & First Name)\n* **Nationalité** (Nationality)\n* **Date et Lieu de Naissance** (Date & Place of Birth)\n* **Numéro de Passeport & Date de Délivrance/Expiration**\n* **Numéro d'Entrée au Maroc** (The 6-to-8 digit alphanumeric code stamped in your passport by border police upon arrival, e.g., *A123456*)\n* **Profession** (Occupation)\n* **Provenance et Destination** (e.g., *Agadir -> Dakhla*)\n* **Marque du Véhicule et Immatriculation** (e.g., *Toyota Prado - 12345-A-26*)\n* **Numéro de Téléphone Marocain** (Local SIM number)\n\nWhen you stop at a southern checkpoint, hand the officer your physical passport along with one printed *Fiche*. The officer will verify your face, thank you warmly for saving them ten minutes of handwriting, and wave you through in under 30 seconds.",
