                "id": "deconstructing-the-400-mad-fine-tiers",
                "heading": "Deconstructing the '400 MAD Fine' Myth: Statutory Tiers & The 50% Immediate Discount",
                "content": "Travel forums are rife with stories of the infamous \"400 Dirham fine\" in Morocco, leading tourists to believe 400 MAD (€37) is either a flat-rate arbitrary penalty or a standardized roadside bribe. Both beliefs are factually incorrect. Under Law 116-14, enacted to curb roadside disputes and incentivize immediate clearing of dockets, Morocco introduced a tiered **Amende Transactionnelle et Forfaitaire (ATF)** system with an automatic abatement (discount) for prompt payment.\n\nIf you pay a traffic violation **immediately on the spot (sur-le-champ)** or within 24 hours at a designated treasury office, the base statutory fine is legally reduced by roughly **43% to 50%**. If you pay within 15 days, the reduction is roughly 28% to 33%. After 15 days, the full base fine applies, and after 30 days without payment, the case is transferred to the King's Prosecutor (*Procureur du Roi*). \n\nThe reason \"400 MAD\" echoes across every travel blog is because it is the exact **discounted on-the-spot rate for a First-Class infraction (700 MAD base fine)**—which covers speeding between 30 and 50 km/h over the limit, crossing a solid white line, failing to stop at a STOP sign, or using a handheld phone while driving.\n\nHere is the exact forensic breakdown of Moroccan speeding and traffic fines under Law 116-14:\n\n| Infraction Class & Speed Excess | Base Fine (16–30 Days) | Paid Within 15 Days | Paid Immediately (Same Day) |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Class 3:** Speeding **< 20 km/h** over limit (after margin), no seatbelt, helmet fault | 300 MAD (€28) | 200 MAD (€18.50) | **150 MAD (€14)** |\n| **Class 2:** Speeding **20 to < 30 km/h** over limit, driving in breakdown lane | 500 MAD (€46) | 350 MAD (€32.50) | **300 MAD (€28)** |\n| **Class 1:** Speeding **30 to < 50 km/h** over limit, red light, STOP sign, solid line, phone in hand | 700 MAD (€65) | 500 MAD (€46) | **400 MAD (€37)** |\n| **Délit (Criminal Offense):** Speeding **≥ 50 km/h** over limit | **4,000 to 8,000 MAD** | *No Discount* | *Immediate License Seizure & Court* |\n\nUnderstanding this table shifts your entire roadside negotiation dynamic. If a Gendarme clocks you at 75 km/h in a 60 km/h zone, your retained speed after the 6 km/h tolerance is 69 km/h (+9 km/h over). That is a **Class 3 infraction**, meaning your immediate legal fine is **150 MAD**, *not* 400 MAD. Sometimes, an officer may verbally quote \"400 Dirhams\" out of habit or to test if you know the tiers. Politely pointing to the radar readout and stating, *\"Mon Adjudant, la vitesse retenue est inférieure à 20 km/h au-dessus de la limite, c'est une contravention de troisième classe à 150 Dirhams,\"* immediately signals that you know Law 116-14 inside out.",
