                "content": "What happens when you are driving from [Casablanca](/locations/casablanca) to [Marrakech](/locations/marrakech) at night, fail to notice a 100 km/h zone before the Settat toll plaza, and see the bright white-or-red strobe flash of a fixed automated radar? \n\nUnlike mobile Gendarmerie checkpoints where you are stopped 400 meters down the road, **fixed automated radars (Radars Fixes) do not trigger immediate roadside stops**. Instead, the infraction enters the centralized digital pipeline of NARSA in Rabat.\n\n### The Legal Pipeline of a Rental Car Radar Flash (Law 116-14)\n1. **Capture & Processing (24 to 72 Hours):** The Mesta Fusion tower transmits the encrypted photo of the license plate to NARSA's automated processing center. Optical Character Recognition (OCR) matches the plate against the national vehicle registry, identifying the rental company as the legal owner.\n2. **Digital Notification to the Fleet Owner:** Through the dedicated NARSA corporate portal (*Infractions Routières*), the rental agency receives an electronic notice of the violation, including the exact timestamp, GPS location, road code, measured speed, and retained speed.\n3. **Driver Identification Declaration (Déclaration d'Identité du Conducteur):** Under Moroccan law, the rental agency is not liable for the fine or the license points—the contracted driver at that specific minute is. The agency legally submits your rental contract details, passport number, and foreign driving license number to the Ministry of Transport within the statutory window.\n\n### How the Fine is Settled Without Industry Scams\nIn the unregulated grey market of Moroccan car rentals, predatory agencies wait until you return the car at the airport, claim their \"system shows 3 radar flashes,\" and demand 1,200 MAD in cash without showing a single piece of government evidence—or worse, freeze €500 from your security deposit for 60 days \"just in case a radar ticket arrives.\"\n\n**Here is the forensic ZwinCar standard and what you have the legal right to expect:**\n* **Verifiable Proof on Infractions.narsa.gov.ma:** No rental agency can demand money for a fixed radar flash without providing the official NARSA Infraction Notice number, the exact timestamp, and the photographic/portal screenshot showing the plate and speed.\n* **Administrative Handling vs. Direct Payment:** When a fixed radar fine is reassigned to a foreign driver's identity, the official fine notice is legally registered under your passport number in the Moroccan national system. If left unpaid, it flags at border control or police databases upon your next entry into the Kingdom. \n* **Immediate Resolution Option:** If a fixed radar flash logs into the NARSA portal before the end of your rental period, a transparent agency will show you the exact portal entry and allow you to settle the discounted ATF amount (150, 300, or 400 MAD) plus a minimal, pre-disclosed administrative processing fee, providing you with the digital payment confirmation from the *Trésorerie Générale du Royaume (TGR)*.",
