                "id": "exact-adm-toll-tariffs-2026",
                "heading": "2026 ADM Toll Cost Audit: Exact Tariffs for Major Moroccan Routes",
                "content": "ADM calculates tolls based on three strict vehicle classification tiers. **99% of standard passenger rental cars—including compact hatchbacks (Renault Clio 5, Peugeot 208) and mid-size SUVs (Hyundai Tucson, Dacia Duster)—fall strictly into Class 1.**\n\n### Official ADM Vehicle Classification Rules\n* **Class 1 (*Véhicules Légers*):** Any two-axle vehicle with an overall height of less than 1.30 meters measured vertically at the front axle. Roof boxes, surfboards, or luggage racks mounted behind the front axle do not alter Class 1 status.\n* **Class 2 (*Véhicules Intermédiaires*):** Two-axle vehicles with a front-axle height equal to or exceeding 1.30 meters (e.g., Ford Transit vans, Fiat Ducato campers, or passenger cars towing a single-axle trailer).\n* **Class 3 (*Poids Lourds*):** Any vehicle or combination with 3 or more axles.\n\n### 2026 Class 1 & Class 2 Route Tariff Matrix\nThe following table documents exact cumulative toll costs across Morocco’s primary tourist and business corridors, segmented by toll booths encountered along the route.\n\n| Highway Corridor | Route Code | Distance | Toll Plazas Encountered | Class 1 Tariff (MAD / EUR) | Class 2 Tariff (MAD / EUR) |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Casablanca → Rabat** | A1 | 87 km | Bouznika (Open) | **23 MAD** (€2.15) | **33 MAD** (€3.05) |\n| **Casablanca → Marrakech** | A3 | 242 km | Bouskoura (Open) + Berrechid–Marrakech Palmeraie (Closed) | **82 MAD** (€7.60) | **135 MAD** (€12.50) |\n| **Casablanca → Tangier** | A1 + A5 | 338 km | Bouznika + Kenitra–Tangier East (Closed) | **136 MAD** (€12.60) | **219 MAD** (€20.30) |\n| **Rabat → Tangier** | A5 | 250 km | Salé/Kenitra → Tangier East (Closed) | **113 MAD** (€10.50) | **186 MAD** (€17.20) |\n| **Marrakech → Agadir** | A3 | 255 km | Loudaya → Amskroud (Closed) | **72 MAD** (€6.65) | **126 MAD** (€11.65) |\n| **Rabat → Fes** | A2 | 207 km | Sidi Allal El Bahraoui → Fes West (Closed) | **69 MAD** (€6.40) | **108 MAD** (€10.00) |\n| **Fes → Oujda** | A2 | 320 km | Fes East → Oujda (Closed) | **99 MAD** (€9.15) | **156 MAD** (€14.45) |\n| **Casablanca → El Jadida** | A1 (South) | 98 km | Had Soualem + Tnine Chtouka + El Jadida | **33 MAD** (€3.05) | **51 MAD** (€4.70) |\n\n### The Casablanca Bypass (Contournement de Casablanca) Micro-Tolls\nDrivers transiting from Rabat (A1) toward Marrakech (A3) or Mohammed V Airport (CMN) without entering downtown Casablanca must utilize the **A101 Bypass** via the Tit Mellil interchange. This bypass operates on micro-tolls ranging from **6 MAD to 13 MAD** depending on your specific exit (Berrechid North vs. Bouskoura). Always keep a dedicated stash of 5, 10, and 20 MAD coins in your center console; handing a 200 MAD banknote for a 7 MAD toll at Tit Mellil causes severe friction with attendants who frequently run out of small change.",
