                "id": "pompiste-etiquette-tipping-and-ancillary-services",
                "heading": "Pompiste Etiquette: Tipping Matrix, Tire Pressure & Windshield Cleaning",
                "content": "Moroccan gas stations operate as multi-service automotive hubs, typically employing separate personnel for fuel dispensing (*le pompiste*), tire maintenance (*le pneumatique* / *vulcanisateur*), and café service. Understanding the financial micro-culture eliminates awkward interactions and prevents tourist overtipping.\n\n### The Zero-Verification Pump Reset Rule\nBefore the attendant inserts the nozzle into your tank, watch them hang up the handle from the previous customer and listen for the mechanical click or digital beep that resets the LCD screen to **0.00 MAD / 0.00 Litres**. If you ask for \"200 Dirhams of Gasoil,\" sophisticated modern pumps allow the attendant to type `200` on the keypad on the side of the dispenser, causing the pump to cut off automatically at the exact dirham.\n\n### The Exact Tipping Matrix\nTipping in Morocco is not calculated as a percentage of the fuel bill; it is a flat micro-payment tied strictly to manual labor performed beyond pulling the pump trigger.\n\n| Service Performed | Who to Pay | Exact Local Tip (MAD) | Euro Equivalent | Forensic Protocol |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Fueling Only (No Extras)** | Pompiste | **0 to 2 MAD** | €0.00 – €0.18 | No tip is expected by locals for simple fueling. Rounding up a 198 MAD bill to 200 MAD is polite. |\n| **Fueling + Windshield Squeegee** | Pompiste | **2 to 5 MAD** | €0.18 – €0.46 | Hand a 5 MAD coin directly to the attendant after they clean the front and rear glass. |\n| **Tire Pressure Check (Gonflage)** | Tire Specialist / Pompiste | **3 to 5 MAD** | €0.28 – €0.46 | Always check pressure when tires are cold. Typical Dacia/Renault load is 2.2 to 2.4 Bar. |\n| **Puncture Repair (Tubeless Plug)** | Station Vulcanisateur | **20 to 30 MAD** (Fixed Fee) | €1.85 – €2.80 | This is a commercial service inside the station garage bay (*Lavage / Pneumatique*). |\n| **Restroom Attendant (Dame Pipi)** | Cleaning Attendant | **1 to 2 MAD** | €0.09 – €0.18 | Only applicable if an attendant is actively cleaning and handing out paper towels at the entrance. |\n\n### Managing the Card vs. Tip Dilemma\nIf you pay for your fuel via credit card, **you cannot add a tip to the TPE card terminal**. The CMI banking system does not support post-authorization tip adjustments at fuel stations, and the station owner will never cash out a card overpayment to a pump worker. Keep a small stash of **1, 2, and 5 MAD coins** in your center console ashtray specifically for attendants and parking guards (*gardiens*).",
                "callout": {
                    "type": "tip",
                    "text": "Politely decline if a pompiste offers to check your engine oil, brake fluid, or coolant ('Vérifier le niveau d'huile ?') on a modern rental car. They are incentivized by commission to sell generic station mineral oil that does not meet OEM synthetic specifications."
                }
