                "answer": "No, driving from Fes to Chefchaouen after dark is strongly discouraged. The R408 and N13 lack road lighting, reflective cat's-eyes are missing on several curves, and unlit pedestrians, donkeys, and agricultural tractors frequently occupy the outer lanes near rural villages like Khenichet and Ain Dorbane. Always depart Fes no later than 14:00 to arrive in Chefchaouen before sunset."
