                "id": "rak-terminal-1-2-exit-architecture",
                "heading": "Terminal 1 & 2 Exit Architecture: Why the 'In-Terminal Desk' is a Bottleneck",
                "content": "Marrakech Menara Airport (RAK), operated by the *Office National Des Aéropports* (ONDA), processes over 6.9 million passengers annually through an infrastructure originally calibrated for 4.5 million. While flight boarding passes designate Terminal 1 or Terminal 2, all international arriving passengers are funneled through a single, unified DGSN (*Direction Générale de la Sûreté Nationale*) passport control hall and customs exit located in Terminal 1.\n\nWhen three or more narrow-body aircraft (typically Ryanair, EasyJet, and Transavia from European hubs) land within the peak 14:00–17:30 window, the customs exit discharges approximately 550 passengers simultaneously into the arrivals concourse. Directly outside the sliding glass doors of the customs zone sit 14 sub-leased ONDA car rental booths. Because these physical kiosks measure less than 6 square meters each, they are staffed by a maximum of two agents per brand.\n\nProcessing a single legacy car rental agreement at an ONDA booth requires an average of 14 to 18 minutes. This duration is dictated by manual passport transcription onto paper *carnets*, upsell pressure for excess waiver policies, and slow GPRS cellular handshakes on legacy *Centre Monétique Interbancaire* (CMI) payment terminals. If you are seventh in line at an international broker franchise desk, your mathematical wait time before even seeing the vehicle is between 98 and 126 minutes.\n\nFurthermore, vehicles belonging to in-terminal booth operators are not parked outside the terminal doors. Once your paperwork is finalized inside Terminal 1, you are handed a key tag and instructed to drag your luggage across the main traffic lanes into the unlit back sectors of Parking P1 or P2 to locate an attendant. \n\n| Operational Metric | Legacy ONDA In-Terminal Booth | Direct Parking P2 Mobile Handover (ZwinCar Protocol) |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Average Wait Time (Peak Arrival)** | 75 to 115 minutes | 0 to 8 minutes (Pre-staged agent) |\n| **Airport Concession Surcharge** | 350 – 450 MAD (€32 – €41) hidden in fees | 0 MAD (Standard ONDA P2 parking ticket only) |\n| **Contract Preparation** | Manual entry at desk upon arrival | Pre-filled digitally via WhatsApp 24h prior |\n| **CMI Deposit Hold Requirement** | 8,000 – 18,000 MAD (€740 – €1,660) | 0 MAD to 3,000 MAD (Transparent / Optional) |\n| **Inspection Lighting Conditions** | Unassisted in dim parking rows | Guided LED-assisted 16-point forensic check |\n\nBy shifting your mental model away from the physical booth toward a pre-authenticated Parking P2 mobile meet-and-greet, you eliminate the single largest friction point in Moroccan travel logistics. Under Moroccan consumer protection Law 31-08, any mandatory 'Airport Service Fee' (*Frais d'Aéroport*) must be explicitly itemized prior to booking; however, third-party aggregators routinely bury the 400 MAD (€37) ONDA concession levy inside the fine print, collecting it forcibly at the desk before releasing the keys.",
