                "id": "navigating-parking-p2-meetup-protocol",
                "heading": "Navigating to Parking P2: Exact Walking Coordinates & Handover Protocol",
                "content": "Executing a seamless vehicle pickup at Marrakech Menara Airport requires understanding the exact spatial geometry of the external esplanade. Upon clearing the green customs channel (*Rien à Déclarer*) in Terminal 1, you will pass the currency exchange booths (where spread rates are an unfavorable 8% to 11% below the Bank Al-Maghrib interbank rate) and exit through the primary automatic sliding doors onto the covered external pedestrian walkway.\n\n**Step-by-Step Navigation from Customs Exit to Parking P2:**\n\n1. **Clear the Terminal Apron (0 – 40 meters):** Walk straight ahead through the main exit doors beneath the architectural geometric canopy. Ignore the aggressive taxi touts on your immediate right (who routinely demand 200 to 300 MAD for a journey regulated at 70 MAD daytime / 105 MAD nighttime).\n2. **Cross the Drop-off Lane (40 – 90 meters):** Proceed across the wide zebra crossing that bisects the active vehicular drop-off lane. Keep your luggage securely in front of you; this lane is monitored by the *Gendarmerie Royale* and automated ANPR cameras enforcing a strict 3-minute drop-off limit.\n3. **Enter the Parking Esplanade (90 – 180 meters):** Directly ahead lies the divided parking complex. **Parking P1** is positioned to your left (facing Terminal 1), while **Parking P2** is positioned to your right (extending in front of Terminal 2 and the modular prayer room).\n4. **Locate the Handover Zone (Rows C to F):** Enter Parking P2 via the central pedestrian spine. Regulated mobile fleet operators stage their vehicles in Rows C, D, E, and F, immediately adjacent to the automated ONDA payment kiosks and the solar-shaded canopies.\n\nWhen utilizing a pre-verified mobile handover protocol like ZwinCar, your assigned fleet logistics officer tracks your inbound flight's ADS-B transponder data (via Flightradar24). The vehicle—such as a Renault Clio 5 Auto or Dacia Duster 4x4—is driven into Parking P2 exactly 20 minutes after your aircraft touches down on Runway 10/28. \n\nThis precise timing is governed by ONDA's automated barrier tariff structure:\n* **0 to 15 minutes:** Free grace period (insufficient for a thorough legal vehicle inspection).\n* **15 to 60 minutes:** 10 MAD (€0.92).\n* **1 to 2 hours:** 20 MAD (€1.85).\n* **2 to 4 hours:** 30 MAD (€2.77).\n* **Up to 24 hours:** 65 MAD (€6.00).\n\nEnsure your agent hands you the magnetic striped ONDA entry ticket upon completing the handover. You will need to insert this ticket into the automated exit bollard within 15 minutes of validation. If the agent has been waiting for over an hour due to border control delays, confirm upfront whether the 10–20 MAD parking exit fee is covered by the agency (standard practice for reputable operators) or requires exact dirham coins at the barrier.",
