                "id": "forensic-vehicle-inspection-law-52-05",
                "heading": "The 12-Minute P2 Forensic Vehicle & Document Audit (Law 52-05 Compliance)",
                "content": "Once you meet your fleet coordinator in Parking P2, do not rush to load your suitcases and drive off. Under the Moroccan Highway Code (*Code de la Route*, promulgated by Dahir 1-10-07 as Law 52-05 and amended by Law 116-14), criminal and civil liability for operating an unroadworthy or improperly documented vehicle falls directly on the driver behind the wheel at the moment of a *Gendarmerie Royale* or *Sûreté Nationale* checkpoint—not on the rental agency.\n\nBefore signing the *Contrat de Location* or authorizing any payment, execute this mandatory 12-minute forensic audit right in the Parking P2 bay:\n\n### 1. The Mandatory Document Pouch (*Pochette Grise*)\nDemand to inspect the physical folder kept in the glovebox. Photocopies without an original municipal legalization stamp (*Copie Certifiée Conforme*) are invalid at rural checkpoints outside Marrakech (such as the N9 route toward Ouarzazate or the A3 motorway toll plaza at Sidi Bou Othmane). Verify these four documents:\n* **Carte Grise (Certificat d'Immatriculation):** Check the magnetic card or Temporary Circulation Certificate (*Récépissé de Dépôt*). Ensure the license plate matches the physical bumper plates and that the usage classification authorizes rental (*Location sans chauffeur*).\n* **Attestation d'Assurance:** Inspect the validity dates down to the exact hour. A policy expiring at 23:59 three days into your seven-day trip will result in immediate vehicle impoundment (*Fourrière*) and a 1,400 MAD (€130) statutory fine under Law 52-05.\n* **TSAV / Vignette (Taxe Spéciale Annuelle sur les Véhicules):** Verify the annual tax receipt for the current calendar year.\n* **Visite Technique:** Mandatory for any rental vehicle older than 12 months. Confirm the inspection stamp is active.\n\n### 2. Mechanical & Bodywork Telemetry\nMarrakech's intense solar radiation and abrasive desert dust degrade rubber and glass rapidly. Walk around the vehicle recording a continuous 4K smartphone video (60 fps) with your flash LED turned on, even during daylight under the P2 solar canopies:\n* **Windshield & Optics:** Film the lower windshield periphery carefully. A 3mm stone chip near the wiper cowling will expand into a 40cm thermal crack the moment you blast cold air conditioning against 42°C glass. If unrecorded on the *État des Lieux* diagram, unscrupulous desks charge 2,500 to 4,500 MAD (€230–€415) for OEM glass replacement.\n* **Tire Sidewalls & DOT Codes:** Inspect all four tires for sidewall bulges (*hernies*) caused by median impacts on Avenue Mohammed VI. Ensure tread depth exceeds the legal 1.6mm minimum. Open the trunk floor and verify the presence of an inflated spare wheel (*roue de secours*) or functional compressor kit, a lug wrench (*clé démonte-roue*), a jack (*cric*), a reflective safety vest (*gilet fluorescent*), and a warning triangle (*triangle de pré-signalisation*). Missing safety triangles trigger an immediate 300 MAD on-the-spot fine (*Amende Transactionnelle et Forfaitaire* - ATF) during police checks.\n* **AdBlue & Fuel Level Calibration:** On modern diesel fleets (e.g., Dacia Sandero Stepway dCi, Dacia Duster 4x4, Renault Clio 5 Blue dCi), turn the ignition to accessory mode and verify no 'Check AdBlue / Antipollution' warning illuminates. Photograph the digital fuel bar count alongside the exact odometer reading.",
