                "id": "cmi-terminal-pre-authorization-deposit-mechanics",
                "heading": "CMI Terminal Architecture: Deposits, Pre-Authorizations, and Franchise Traps",
                "content": "Upon arriving at Tangier Airport (TNG) or meeting your delivery agent at Tanger Ville Marina, the financial mechanics of your vehicle handover are governed by the **Centre Monétique Interbancaire (CMI)**, Morocco’s centralized payment processing clearinghouse. Understanding how CMI terminals process foreign plastic is critical to avoiding sudden pickup refusals.\n\nMoroccan rental agencies execute security deposits (*Caution*) using an **ISO 8583 Pre-Authorization command (MTI 0100)**. Unlike a standard retail capture, an MTI 0100 hold freezes funds on an open line of credit for up to 21 banking days without settling the transaction. Because this requires an unencumbered credit ledger, CMI terminals automatically analyze the **Bank Identification Number (BIN)**—the first 6 to 8 digits of your card.\n\nIf you present a Debit Card (Visa Electron, Mastercard Debit, Revolut, Monzo, N26, Wise, or North American checking-linked debit cards), the CMI terminal reads the debit BIN flag and rejects the MTI 0100 pre-authorization command. Even if you hold €20,000 in liquid checking funds, a standard airport franchise desk cannot execute a temporary block on a debit BIN.\n\nWhen a debit card fails at TNG Terminal 1, global franchises enforce a coercive binary ultimatum:\n1. **Forced Sale Charge (Vente Directe):** They swipe your debit card as a live merchandise purchase for 10,000 to 20,000 MAD (€925–€1,850). You immediately lose 3% to 5% on currency conversion spreads, and upon returning the car, you lose another 3% to 5% when the refund is processed 14 to 30 days later.\n2. **Mandatory In-House SCDW:** They refuse to release the vehicle unless you purchase their non-refundable counter Super Collision Damage Waiver at 250 to 380 MAD (€23–€35) per day, completely negating any third-party insurance you bought online through booking brokers.\n\n| Vehicle Category | Representative Fleet Model | Standard Franchise Hold (MAD) | Transparent Local Deposit / SCDW |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Economy / Compact** | `dacia-sandero-stepway` | 8,000 – 12,000 MAD (€740–€1,110) | 0 – 3,000 MAD (€0–€275) |\n| **Automatic Hatchback** | `renault-clio-5-auto` | 10,000 – 14,000 MAD (€925–€1,300) | 0 – 4,000 MAD (€0–€370) |\n| **Mid-Size SUV** | `hyundai-tucson-auto` | 16,000 – 25,000 MAD (€1,480–€2,315) | 0 – 6,000 MAD (€0–€555) |\n\n**The Chèque de Garantie Prohibition:**\nIf renting from unvetted street brokers near Boulevard Mohammed VI, never sign a blank Moroccan bank check (*Chèque de Garantie*) or an undated commercial promissory note. Under **Article 316 of the Moroccan Commercial Code (Code de Commerce)**, issuing a check without immediate liquid provision—or signing a blank check as a security guarantee—is a strict-liability criminal offense punishable by 1 to 5 years imprisonment. Always utilize structured, compliant agencies such as ZwinCar that accept regulated debit structures, transparent cash deposits with signed counter-receipts (*Reçu de Cautionnement*), or true zero-excess coverage.",
